"parts":[{"text":"நசைவர்","lemma":"நசைவர்","gloss":"those who desire / friends"},{"text":"க்கு","lemma":"க்கு","gloss":"dative suffix"}],"gloss":"to those who desire"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அளந்து","parts":[{"text":"அள","lemma":"அள","gloss":"to measure"},{"text":"ந்து","lemma":"ந்து","gloss":"past participle suffix"}],"gloss":"having measured"},{"surface":"கொடை","parts":[{"text":"கொடை","lemma":"கொடை","gloss":"giving"}],"gloss":"giving"},{"surface":"அறியா","parts":[{"text":"அறி","lemma":"அறி","gloss":"to know"},{"text":"ஆ","lemma":"ஆ","gloss":"negative participle suffix"}],"gloss":"not knowing"},{"surface":"ஈகை","parts":[{"text":"ஈகை","lemma":"ஈகை","gloss":"generosity"}],"gloss":"generosity"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மணி","parts":[{"text":"மணி","lemma":"மணி","gloss":"sapphire"}],"gloss":"sapphire"},{"surface":"வரை","parts":[{"text":"வரை","lemma":"வரை","gloss":"mountain"}],"gloss":"mountain"},{"surface":"அன்ன","parts":[{"text":"அன்ன","lemma":"அன்ன","gloss":"like"}],"gloss":"like"},{"surface":"மாஅயோனே","parts":[{"text":"மாஅயோனே","lemma":"மாஅயோனே","gloss":"dark-complexioned one"}],"gloss":"dark-complexioned one","split_unverified":true}]}],"literal":"In the moving nature of Krittika's division / in the dense darkness of midnight / starting from the root of the bent palmyra (Anuradha) / to the end of the pond (Kulam) star, as water dried up / in the high expanse of the Panguni month / the first asterism shifted its position / the established asterism rose up opposite to it / the ancient asterism sank in its place / not going westward, not approaching northward / as a lamp to the ocean-girt earth / with dense fire spreading, rising up against the wind / a star fell from the sky / seeing that, we and others, various suppliants / of the king of the good country with sounding waterfall drums / said, \"If he is without illness, it is indeed good, oh!\" / with broken hearts, with shrinking minds spreading grief / we feared; the seventh day came today indeed / the strong elephants sleep with their trunks placed down / the tightly bound drums roll with torn drumheads / the protective white umbrellas wither with broken staffs / the wind-swift spirited horses languish without gait / because he reached the world of the gods / being a firm support to the bright-bangled women / did he forget his companion group of friends? / with power to bind enemies, to those who desire / giving without measuring / like a sapphire mountain, the dark-complexioned one!","translation":"In the deep darkness of midnight, in the division of the moving Krittika star, starting from the root of the bent palmyra star (Anuradha) to the end of the pond star (Kulam) as if water dried up, in the high expanse of the sky in the month of Panguni, the first star shifted its position, the established star rose opposite to it, and the ancient star sank in its place. Without moving westward or approaching northward, like a lamp to the ocean-girt earth, spreading dense fire and rising against the wind, a meteor fell from the sky. Seeing that, we and other suppliants of the king of the land of drum-like waterfalls prayed, \"Oh, if only he is free from illness, it would be well!\" With broken hearts and shrinking minds, we feared; and today, the seventh day has arrived. The strong elephants sleep with their trunks laid down, the tightly bound drums roll with torn drumheads, the protective white umbrellas wither with broken staffs, and the wind-swift spirited horses languish without gait. Because he has reached the world of the gods, did he, who was a firm support to his bright-bangled women, forget his companion group of friends? He who had the power to bind enemies, who gave to those who desired without measuring, the dark-complexioned one who stood like a sapphire mountain!","modern":"நள்ளிரவின் அடர்ந்த காரிருளில், கார்த்திகை விண்மீன் கூட்டத்தில், வளைந்த பனை போன்ற அனுஷ விண்மீனை முதலாகக் கொண்டு குளத்து விண்மீனின் இறுதி வரை நீர் வற்றுவது போல, பங்குனி மாதத்து உயர்ந்த வானத்தில், முதன்மை விண்மீன் தன் நிலை மாறியது. அதற்கு எதிராக நிலைபெற்ற விண்மீன் மேலே எழுந்தது. பழமையான விண்மீன் தன் துறையில் மூழ்கியது. அது மேற்கே செல்லாமலும் வடக்கே நெருங்காமலும், கடல் சூழ்ந்த உலகிற்கு விளக்கு போல, நெருப்புப் பிழம்பைப் பரப்பி, காற்றுக்கு எதிராகப் பொங்கி, வானத்திலிருந்து ஒரு விண்மீன் வீழ்ந்தது. அதனைக் கண்டு, அருவிகள் முரசு போல ஒலிக்கும் நல்ல நாட்டுக்குத் தலைவனான மன்னன் நோயின்றி வாழ வேண்டும் என்று நாங்களும் பிற இரவலர்களும் வேண்டினோம். உடைந்த நெஞ்சத்தோடு அஞ்சிய எங்களுக்கு ஏழாம் நாள் இன்றே வந்துவிட்டது. வலிமையான யானைகள் தும்பிக்கையைத் தரை மேல் வைத்து உறங்குகின்றன. முரசுகள் கண் கிழிந்து உருளுகின்றன. வெண்கொற்றக் குடைகள் காம்புகள் முறிந்து காய்ந்து கிடக்கின்றன. குதிரைகள் ஓட்டமின்றி வாடுகின்றன. ஏனெனில், பகைவரைப் பிணிக்கும் ஆற்றல் கொண்டவனும், இரவலர்க்கு எல்லையின்றி வாரி வழங்கியவனுமான, நீலமணி மலை போன்ற கரிய நிறமுடைய மன்னன் தேவருலகம் எய்திவிட்டான். தன் ஒளிரும் வளையல் அணிந்த மகளிர்க்குத் துணையாக இருந்த அவன், தன் நண்பர் கூட்டத்தை மறந்துவிட்டானோ?","explanation":"This poem is a poignant expression of grief (kaiyaṟunilai) by the poet Koodaloor Kizhar on the death of the Chera king Yanaikatchei Mantharanjeral Irumporai. The poet describes a terrifying astronomical event he witnessed: a meteor falling from the sky during the month of Panguni, which was traditionally regarded as a dire omen for the king's life. Fearing the worst, the poet and other bards prayed for the king's well-being, but exactly seven days later, the omen proved true, and the king passed away. The poem vividly depicts the state of the palace after the king's death, where royal elephants sleep in sorrow, war drums lie torn and broken, and swift horses stand listless. The king is praised for his boundless generosity and compared to a majestic sapphire mountain, leaving his subjects and companions in deep despair.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.5],[0.5,0.8],[0.8,1.0],[1.0,1.4],[1.4,2.2],[2.2,2.5],[2.5,2.6],[2.6,2.9],[2.9,3.35],[3.58,3.81],[3.81,4.04],[4.04,5.4],[5.4,6.0],[6.0,6.1],[6.1,6.6],[